#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133479 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133916 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40486856-137f-55c4-8464-f99e7e1c659f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Mixed Integral"}] :question/id #uuid "1b09be02-1515-5277-bac6-9289b9dbe371" :question/math-academy-id "e-11506" :question/problem "Evaluate the mixed integral \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_D \\left[ \\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}} 2y\\: \\mathrm{d}y \\right ]  \\mathrm{d}A,\n$$\n\ngiven that $D$ is the region in the $xz$-plane bounded by the lines $z=0,$ $x= 1$ and the line $z =x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}2y\\,dy]dA & ={∬}_{D}[{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=\\sqrt{x}}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate this double integral, we plot $D$ as a type I plane region in the $xz$-plane.\n\n![](images/1d/1d102b63c3deb8121ea88cdc994b9410cf28f9c3bb29abc5ea4a14d7e1e7c389.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, to evaluate our double integral as a repeated integral over this region, we integrate with respect to $z$ and then with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}x\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x[z]_{z=0}^{z=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133480 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133917 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf29db1b-f47b-53de-b31d-e4da1d0a9e5f" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Triple Integral as a Mixed or Repeated Integral"}] :question/id #uuid "216b16aa-d279-519e-a749-b9fd5517a6db" :question/math-academy-id "e-11507" :question/problem "Find the missing limits in the repeated integral below\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint \\limits_{R} f(x,y,z) \\: \\textrm{d}V \n= \n\\int_{\\ast}^{\\ast} \n\\int_{\\ast}^{\\ast} \n\\int_{\\ast}^{\\ast} \nf(x,y,z) \\: \\mathrm{d}y \\: \\mathrm{d}z \\: \\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the type III region defined as\n\n$$\nR=\\left\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: -3 \\leq x \\leq 3, \\: x \\leq z \\leq 2x+2, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq z+xz \\right\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A type III region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{ (x,y,z)  \\: : \\: (x,z) \\in D, \\: u_1(x,z) \\leq y \\leq u_2(x,z) \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type III region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/06/0603bed12c6af74e46544d8bebc52362aed95a9a5ad7418ea4faaf228f3b5241.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type III region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\iiint\\limits_{R} f(x,y,z)\\,\\textrm d V = \\iint\\limits_{D} \\left[\\int_{u_1(x,z)}^{u_2(x,z)} f(x,y,z)\\,\\textrm d y \\right] \\,\\textrm d A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nu_1(x,z) = 0, \\qquad u_2(x,z)  = z+xz.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint \\limits_{S} f(x,y,z) \\: \\textrm{d}V \n= \n\\iint\\limits_{D} \\left[ \\int_{0}^{z+xz} f(x,y,z) \\: \\mathrm{d}y \\right] \\mathrm{d}A.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD =\\left\\{ (x,z) \\: : \\: -3 \\leq x \\leq 3, \\: x \\leq z \\leq 2x+2 \\right\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by expressing the double integral over $D$ as a repeated integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{z+xz}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA & ={\\int }_{-3}^{3}{\\int }_{x}^{2x+2}[{\\int }_{0}^{z+xz}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dz\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{3}{\\int }_{x}^{2x+2}{\\int }_{0}^{z+xz}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133483 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133923 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4693bb81-f299-50fa-9cbd-3a5bb1c90da9" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Over a Type III Region"}] :question/id #uuid "72b1ac41-be39-5a51-bc0c-738d36cdb81b" :question/math-academy-id "e-12378" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint\\limits_R 8xy  \\: \\mathrm{d}V\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR = \\left\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: (x,z) \\in D, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq \\sqrt x \\right\\},\n$$\n\nand $D$ is the finite region in $xz$-plane enclosed between the $x$-axis, the line $x=1,$ and the line $z=x$ in the first quadrant." :question/worked-solution "Writing down our triple integral as a mixed integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint \\limits_{R} 8xy \\, \\textrm{d}V\n=\n\\iint\\limits_D \\left[ \\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}} 8xy\\: \\mathrm{d}y \\right ]  \\mathrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}8xy\\,dy]dA & ={∬}_{D}4x[{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=\\sqrt{x}}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}4x(x-0)\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}4{x}^{2}\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now evaluate this double integral over the region $D$ in the $xz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](images/1d/1d102b63c3deb8121ea88cdc994b9410cf28f9c3bb29abc5ea4a14d7e1e7c389.png)\n\nWe can evaluate our double integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}4{x}^{2}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}4{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4{x}^{2}[z]_{z=0}^{z=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4{x}^{2}(x-0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{x}^{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & ={1}^{4}-0 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133485 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133925 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1889f67-327c-5e6e-b646-5bd58a244778" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing and Evaluating Triple Integrals Over Type III Regions From Diagrams"}] :question/id #uuid "21fdb746-8831-5b97-acf0-5a14a2e34980" :question/math-academy-id "e-12400" :question/problem "![](images/b0/b0817c04ee57a8352f8f56a4c232668d415c1573e37a81729752d65c0fb9e1c1.png)\n\n \n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n$\\displaystyle \\iiint\\limits_R 36z^2  \\: \\mathrm{d}V$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the right one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](images/05/0584c95ae22135288f08fc8d0ef472aae867eccecf958c65e82eb311da69a1ae.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type III region\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: (x,z) \\in D, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 5-x-z \\big\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,z) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq z \\leq 1 \\big\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/36/365451aa395e91cee59199b048ed59ce1fba2ee8ee569fc460ef8fe9bf3bcdfd.png)\n\nHence, the type III representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq z \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 5-x-z \\big\\}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint \\limits_{R} 36z^2 \\: \\textrm{d}V \n= \n\\int_{0}^{1} \\int_{0}^{1} \\int_{0}^{5-x-z} 36z^2 \\: \\mathrm{d}y \\: \\mathrm{d}z \\: \\mathrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{5-x-z}36{z}^{2}\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{5-x-z}36{z}^{2}\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}36{z}^{2}[y]_{y=0}^{y=5-x-z}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}36{z}^{2}(5-x-z)\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(180{z}^{2}-36x{z}^{2}-36{z}^{3})\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(180{z}^{2}-36x{z}^{2}-36{z}^{3})\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}(180{z}^{2}-36x{z}^{2}-36{z}^{3})\\,dz]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[60{z}^{3}-12x{z}^{3}-9{z}^{4}]_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(51-12x)\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(51-12x)\\,dx & =[51x-6{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(51(1)-6(1)^{2})-0 \\\\  & =45\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527911 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133916 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40486856-137f-55c4-8464-f99e7e1c659f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Mixed Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0438c001-4681-59c9-8849-bfb0fea1ea87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527316} {:answer/id #uuid "1fd3f49a-2cb7-53fd-81b2-5b3857da1e8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527377} {:answer/id #uuid "930c7ce8-022d-5e4d-bd0e-9c20804f999e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527598} {:answer/id #uuid "bfadebc0-e9ba-513f-b060-6475dd84329f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527695} {:answer/id #uuid "f5e2d875-4536-53de-bade-39c60d2d073b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527786}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fd3f49a-2cb7-53fd-81b2-5b3857da1e8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527377} :answer-field/id #uuid "07cc355d-4413-59ca-bc08-a5af18b8dff8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527805}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0597a6d4-1752-5cad-a458-a8b2a80e68a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-161666" :question/problem "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}2x\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\ngiven that the region $D$ in the $xz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 2-x\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}2x\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}2x[y]_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I region in the $xz$-plane.\nTherefore, to evaluate our double integral as a repeated integral over this region, we integrate with respect to $z$ and then with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-x}2{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2{x}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2-x}\\,\\text{d}z]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2{x}^{2}{[z]}_{z=0}^{z=2-x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2{x}^{2}(2-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(4{x}^{2}-2{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{32}{3}-8)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527962 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133916 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40486856-137f-55c4-8464-f99e7e1c659f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Mixed Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16859933-75c0-53cc-92d2-abc0eb0131cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527351} {:answer/id #uuid "25582ec9-aea6-53c2-b2a3-0a0449093e1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527391} {:answer/id #uuid "5dbf81b7-4c30-539d-840c-554a9ef51ef3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527485} {:answer/id #uuid "88b8ff89-b6c2-573a-9042-004cee1995e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527574} {:answer/id #uuid "9886d286-2a1c-56a0-abf4-404d3ebfd465" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527618}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88b8ff89-b6c2-573a-9042-004cee1995e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527574} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e152976-df66-5055-a7f1-93a051729b6f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527806}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7dfdc43a-549b-5350-87ba-ec6dde24e325" :question/math-academy-id "q-161689" :question/problem "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}5yz\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\ngiven that the region $D$ in the $xz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le z\\le 2,\\,0\\le x\\le 2-z\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $z$ and $x$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}5yz\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}5z{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{∬}_{D}z(4-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type II region in the $xz$-plane.\nTherefore, to evaluate our double integral as a repeated integral over this region, we integrate with respect to $x$ and then with respect to $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2}{∬}_{D}z(4-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-z}z(4-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}z[{\\int }_{0}^{2-z}(4-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}z \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}z{[(4x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})]}_{x=0}^{x=2-z}\\text{d}z \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}z(4(2-z)-\\frac{(2-z)^{3}}{3})\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{16z}{3}-2{z}^{3}+\\frac{{z}^{4}}{3})\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{[\\frac{8{z}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{z}^{4}}{2}+\\frac{{z}^{5}}{15}]}_{z=0}^{z=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}[\\frac{32}{3}-8+\\frac{32}{15}] \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281307 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133917 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf29db1b-f47b-53de-b31d-e4da1d0a9e5f" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Triple Integral as a Mixed or Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fa5bdff-7005-5ec5-8d80-f8b856c23017" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-z}^{{x}^{2}+z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279010} {:answer/id #uuid "6597255a-aab0-55f2-9ed7-2df3b0c5bd5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-z}^{{x}^{2}+z}[{∬}_{D}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279514} {:answer/id #uuid "7fe1f465-25bf-5d62-ae2b-845bc56fcc26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}+z}^{-z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dz" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279740} {:answer/id #uuid "c9d00fb8-2293-5455-a322-7d10609e79d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}+z}^{-z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280358} {:answer/id #uuid "e0d44e8b-e4d8-593a-a817-7e8b04fb3f94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-z}^{{x}^{2}+z}f(x,y,z)\\,dz]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280583}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2fa5bdff-7005-5ec5-8d80-f8b856c23017" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-z}^{{x}^{2}+z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279010} :answer-field/id #uuid "9575c3e7-857c-5f96-ad84-b47a94df34c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281102}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2f13673d-47ba-5a25-8690-9d3a570aad64" :question/math-academy-id "q-161722" :question/problem "Consider the type III region $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,-z\\le y\\le {x}^{2}+z\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is some finite region in the $xz$-plane. Then,\n\n$$\n{∭}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A type III region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(x,z)\\le y\\le {u}_{2}(x,z)\\}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type III region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/06/0603bed12c6af74e46544d8bebc52362aed95a9a5ad7418ea4faaf228f3b5241.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type III region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,z)}^{{u}_{2}(x,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(x,z)=-z,\\,{u}_{2}(x,z)={x}^{2}+z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-z}^{{x}^{2}+z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527996 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133917 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf29db1b-f47b-53de-b31d-e4da1d0a9e5f" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Triple Integral as a Mixed or Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75b5c8f7-895b-598c-995e-c9969c74ab4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{z}^{2}}^{2+{x}^{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527529} {:answer/id #uuid "7a3b40bd-6ba3-5c6f-a50d-e136b30c1575" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2+{z}^{2}}[{∬}_{D}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527537} {:answer/id #uuid "83b7b59c-3096-5045-b2d3-c5c71c1cede6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2+{z}^{2}}[{∬}_{D}f(x,y,z)\\,dz]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527563} {:answer/id #uuid "8675b4ab-bb5f-5a68-ae4d-857a847c3317" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2+{z}^{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527568} {:answer/id #uuid "f9168d9c-6caa-5d83-8598-aa569821bcca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{2+{z}^{2}}^{{x}^{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527792}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8675b4ab-bb5f-5a68-ae4d-857a847c3317" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2+{z}^{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527568} :answer-field/id #uuid "d16be51a-dcbd-5540-95d0-1d9d605bbc50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527892}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d33bfb77-09ea-5195-a418-173b3296a490" :question/math-academy-id "q-161723" :question/problem "Consider the type III region $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 2+{z}^{2}\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is some finite region in the $xz$-plane. Then,\n\n$$\n{∭}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A type III region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(x,z)\\le y\\le {u}_{2}(x,z)\\}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type III region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/06/0603bed12c6af74e46544d8bebc52362aed95a9a5ad7418ea4faaf228f3b5241.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type III region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,z)}^{{u}_{2}(x,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(x,z)={x}^{2},\\,{u}_{2}(x,z)=2+{z}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2+{z}^{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528004 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133917 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf29db1b-f47b-53de-b31d-e4da1d0a9e5f" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Triple Integral as a Mixed or Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08706535-f622-5555-ba54-c03e78f1bfb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}-2}^{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527323} {:answer/id #uuid "26c0a398-9caf-5cdc-aa61-4b5c9cfff695" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{{x}^{2}+2}^{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}[{∬}_{D}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527395} {:answer/id #uuid "46b4dd8a-b180-55d7-8b32-7bcdc327bc32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}+2}^{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,dz]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527445} {:answer/id #uuid "4ee0672b-4cd4-5352-9169-0c2cf00ab5c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{{x}^{2}-2}^{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}[{∬}_{D}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527460} {:answer/id #uuid "b1546550-e4e4-55ca-8d15-539c770e18bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{{z}^{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527672}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08706535-f622-5555-ba54-c03e78f1bfb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}-2}^{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527323} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ecc2622-9e4d-59da-9d15-d5bdd601e67d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527808}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e1798463-dc83-5fa2-a428-d476acd2c869" :question/math-academy-id "q-161724" :question/problem "Consider the type III region $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,{x}^{2}-2\\le y\\le {x}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is some finite region in the $xz$-plane. Then,\n\n$$\n{∭}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A type III region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(x,z)\\le y\\le {u}_{2}(x,z)\\}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type III region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/06/0603bed12c6af74e46544d8bebc52362aed95a9a5ad7418ea4faaf228f3b5241.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type III region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,z)}^{{u}_{2}(x,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(x,z)={x}^{2}-2,\\,{u}_{2}(x,z)={x}^{2}+{z}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}-2}^{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527918 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133916 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40486856-137f-55c4-8464-f99e7e1c659f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Mixed Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79072c2d-8f08-5f5d-b719-e8897f0003bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527535} {:answer/id #uuid "86d4e147-37c0-5de6-9297-866f2a3e212e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527570} {:answer/id #uuid "9acf82d9-0415-5a81-99b2-8d7595b0a6f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527626} {:answer/id #uuid "d4818782-d4a8-5e32-83a7-0f9ae23058c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527738} {:answer/id #uuid "ea550bee-68b7-502c-8b85-afcf994105bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527766}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79072c2d-8f08-5f5d-b719-e8897f0003bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527535} :answer-field/id #uuid "59fa8c03-9424-5baf-a214-fbd3a612fb42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527842}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0f4e6580-868c-593b-ba50-63aa6d6e6e42" :question/math-academy-id "q-161725" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{x}^{\\sqrt{1-z}}4xy\\,dy]dA,\n$$\n\nEvaluate the repeated integral above given that $D$ is a region in the $xz$-plane bounded by the lines $z=0,$ $x=0,$ and the curve $z+{x}^{2}=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{x}^{\\sqrt{1-z}}4xy\\,dy]dA & ={∬}_{D}2x[{y}^{2}]_{y=x}^{y=\\sqrt{1-z}}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2x(1-z-{x}^{2})\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\,2x(1-z)-2{x}^{3}\\,)\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate this double integral, we plot $D$ as a type I plane region in the $xz$-plane.\n\n![](images/80/8079d8f9796c1f863a515ced0091c1f420318be1c4bfe0eb2da641bddfa426ce.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, to evaluate our double integral as a repeated integral over this region, we integrate with respect to $z$ and then with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(\\,2x(1-z)-2{x}^{3}\\,)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}(\\,2x(1-z)-2{x}^{3}\\,)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(x[-(1-z)^{2}]_{z=0}^{z=1-{x}^{2}}-2{x}^{3}[z]_{z=0}^{z=1-{x}^{2}}\\,)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-{x}^{5}+x-2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{5}+x-2{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{6}{x}^{6}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2})-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281312 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133916 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40486856-137f-55c4-8464-f99e7e1c659f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Mixed Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "361bfe9b-b263-5de7-93b7-f4db26264c8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279065} {:answer/id #uuid "74283afe-9e20-5de9-a9ee-f485a91d9c20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279640} {:answer/id #uuid "78aca257-927d-598a-a519-e0eb2ba39a6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279666} {:answer/id #uuid "7d2dbf0f-2ebb-5bee-a881-105fa780856d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279710} {:answer/id #uuid "9566a15c-dee3-5f61-8f42-b9b8f56fd259" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279920}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9566a15c-dee3-5f61-8f42-b9b8f56fd259" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279920} :answer-field/id #uuid "2eb2ba9a-f03f-55df-8fb0-cec85d841b52" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280919}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4b555d9f-d5f9-558f-a244-86b96b18ac88" :question/math-academy-id "q-161733" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}4zy\\,dy]dA,\n$$\n\nEvaluate the repeated integral above given that $D$ is a region in the $xz$-plane bounded by the lines $z=0,$ $x=2$ and the line $z-x=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}4zy\\,dy]dA & ={∬}_{D}2z[{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=\\sqrt{x}}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2zx\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate this double integral, we plot $D$ as a type I plane region in the $xz$-plane.\n\n![](images/b7/b748f589d7fa773444fc45bdbd1d94a5424bb81c40851f0f0f2542a4f66c0c8d.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, to evaluate our double integral as a repeated integral over this region, we integrate with respect to $z$ and then with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2zx\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}2zx\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x[{z}^{2}]_{z=0}^{z=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =4-0 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281313 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133923 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4693bb81-f299-50fa-9cbd-3a5bb1c90da9" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Over a Type III Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "415161dd-cdcb-5425-acb1-938cd55cb558" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279174} {:answer/id #uuid "7626f571-253c-5ce7-9602-4e73e0d03ae4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279646} {:answer/id #uuid "c7929a24-2bd5-5143-a65f-50417cb26bc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280341} {:answer/id #uuid "d47896b0-3c68-5df1-9e8f-025e32352d5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280465} {:answer/id #uuid "f99e0a64-1e5b-5066-84d8-97275f14d7c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "415161dd-cdcb-5425-acb1-938cd55cb558" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279174} :answer-field/id #uuid "af73b320-686f-5899-8f90-0fd38634d25e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281136}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ff27e038-e43c-5a90-b151-748220a86ed2" :question/math-academy-id "q-161735" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}12y\\,dV\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}\\},\n$$\n\nand $D$ is a finite region in $xz$-plane enclosed between the $x$-axis, the line $x=1,$ and the line $z=x$ in the first quadrant." :question/worked-solution "Writing down our triple integral as a mixed integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}12y\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}12y\\,dy]dA.\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}12y\\,dy]dA & ={∬}_{D}6[{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=\\sqrt{x}}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}6x\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe must now evaluate this double integral over the region $D$ in the $xz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](images/1d/1d102b63c3deb8121ea88cdc994b9410cf28f9c3bb29abc5ea4a14d7e1e7c389.png)\n\n \n\nWe can evaluate our double integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}6x\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}6x\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6x[z]_{z=0}^{z=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[2{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528006 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133923 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4693bb81-f299-50fa-9cbd-3a5bb1c90da9" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Over a Type III Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "565f5262-532c-5e41-8ea0-d94694ac1b53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527472} {:answer/id #uuid "81298f2e-a4cc-5c37-837c-36620a8723f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527560} {:answer/id #uuid "90f1f224-4869-5295-a80b-2af51c894cd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527592} {:answer/id #uuid "a23b2b89-1dca-5af5-9d84-12be328a7e2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527641} {:answer/id #uuid "bfc76cd0-c0a3-5a18-9d90-d4b09fd8e301" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527696}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a23b2b89-1dca-5af5-9d84-12be328a7e2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527641} :answer-field/id #uuid "62352491-31d2-5339-9e42-95ca180169b7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527846}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e4e7d822-5d73-50ee-b641-1c594f9a070a" :question/math-academy-id "q-161738" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}3x\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the type III region given by \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le x,\\,0\\le z\\le 2-x\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}3x\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-x}{\\int }_{0}^{x}3x\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-x}{\\int }_{0}^{x}3x\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-x}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}3x\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-x}3x[y]_{y=0}^{y=x}dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-x}3x(x-0)\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-x}3{x}^{2}\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-x}3{x}^{2}\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3{x}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2-x}\\,\\text{d}z]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3{x}^{2}{[z]}_{z=0}^{z=2-x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3{x}^{2}(2-x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(6{x}^{2}-3{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(6{x}^{2}-3{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & ={[2{x}^{3}-\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(16-12)-0 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528008 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133917 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf29db1b-f47b-53de-b31d-e4da1d0a9e5f" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Triple Integral as a Mixed or Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e42e40e-c96a-58c9-9612-0406917ecf9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z+x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527376} {:answer/id #uuid "30d0159a-b42b-51ba-b22a-df45c14b3437" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2-z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527409} {:answer/id #uuid "934f89a5-9a46-5676-98f1-76182ab85055" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-z-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527599} {:answer/id #uuid "982a8761-3b79-5432-9984-542ac899a03a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527615} {:answer/id #uuid "b43658c4-c0e4-563f-a52d-4334e8d4e468" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2-x-z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b43658c4-c0e4-563f-a52d-4334e8d4e468" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2-x-z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527675} :answer-field/id #uuid "d83fd660-d05c-552a-9c9c-8182ba76ceb4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527894}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ea162333-68ea-5f39-92a3-425dd5b76bfd" :question/math-academy-id "q-161745" :question/problem "$$\n{∭}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{a}^{∗}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{∗}^{b}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx\n$$\n\nThe triple integral above is defined over the type III region given by\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,-2\\le z\\le {x}^{2}+2,\\,-2-z\\le y\\le 2+x+z\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $a-b?$" :question/worked-solution "A type III region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(x,z)\\le y\\le {u}_{2}(x,z)\\}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type III region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/06/0603bed12c6af74e46544d8bebc52362aed95a9a5ad7418ea4faaf228f3b5241.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type III region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,z)}^{{u}_{2}(x,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(x,z)=-2-z,\\,{u}_{2}(x,z)=2+x+z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-2-z}^{2+x+z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,-2\\le z\\le {x}^{2}+2\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by expressing the double integral over $D$ as a repeated integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-2-z}^{2+x+z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-2}^{{x}^{2}+2}[{\\int }_{-2-z}^{2+x+z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dz\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-2}^{{x}^{2}+2}{\\int }_{-2-z}^{2+x+z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na-b=(0)-(2+x+z)=-2-x-z.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281317 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133923 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4693bb81-f299-50fa-9cbd-3a5bb1c90da9" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Over a Type III Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e0673f9-49be-5b89-b056-38db50720c36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278995} {:answer/id #uuid "717da108-6fee-53dd-a64c-56bda00fabfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279621} {:answer/id #uuid "8d059927-b69b-5ea3-a1c9-5cdbd981ac25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279849} {:answer/id #uuid "a5bbe5f5-1301-5da1-a4a3-b42afc64de96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280061} {:answer/id #uuid "d2b7b408-79ac-599e-9d52-7731e5ecb06f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5bbe5f5-1301-5da1-a4a3-b42afc64de96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280061} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c28af51-d8e7-53ee-b355-cdf9be35b210" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281060}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f9e6176f-e02b-5e64-8d69-eb13369492af" :question/math-academy-id "q-161751" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}20y\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the type III region given by \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le 1-{x}^{2},\\,0\\le y\\le 1-x\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2x\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}20y\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}20y\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}[{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}20y\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}[10{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=1-x}dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}10(1-x)^{2}\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}10(1-x)^{2}\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}10(1-x)^{2}\\,dz]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}10(1-x)^{2}[z]_{z=0}^{z=1-{x}^{2}}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}10(1-x)^{2}(1-{x}^{2})dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}10(1-2x+2{x}^{3}-{x}^{4})\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}10(1-2x+2{x}^{3}-{x}^{4})\\,dx & ={[10(x-{x}^{2}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5})]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527914 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133923 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4693bb81-f299-50fa-9cbd-3a5bb1c90da9" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Over a Type III Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b7d98c9-02ac-5603-afb5-66c0e4f344f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527426} {:answer/id #uuid "40bf70c8-60bf-5224-82fd-7ff84ef20808" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527433} {:answer/id #uuid "aa0afc20-5227-5ba6-b5db-de3861c4378d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527656} {:answer/id #uuid "b718d3fb-6237-5710-a206-2a584cc97e02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527683} {:answer/id #uuid "de78bae8-e4d7-569c-a55e-af9dd522c7c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527750}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de78bae8-e4d7-569c-a55e-af9dd522c7c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527750} :answer-field/id #uuid "84189abc-599a-55c9-aabf-a7a75d8a52db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527862}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0bcb5cdc-84fc-59d4-a070-2f4375bf7e4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-161764" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}4xy\\,dV\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,x\\le y\\le \\sqrt{1-z}\\},\n$$\n\nand $D$ is a finite region in $xz$-plane enclosed between the $x$-axis, the $z$-axis, and the curve $z=1-{x}^{2},$ in the first quadrant." :question/worked-solution "Writing down our triple integral as a mixed integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}4xy\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{x}^{\\sqrt{1-z}}4xy\\,dy]dA.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{x}^{\\sqrt{1-z}}4xy\\,dy]dA & ={∬}_{D}2x[{y}^{2}]_{y=x}^{y=\\sqrt{1-z}}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2x(\\,(1-z)-{x}^{2})\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2x(1-z)-2{x}^{3}\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now evaluate this double integral over the region $D$ in the $xz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](images/95/95a2b4e28dbfae5ce447b3b975b2f74bf04883441217f42a24636970948402a0.png)\n\n  \n\nWe can evaluate our double integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2x(1-z)-2{x}^{3}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-z}}2x(1-z)-2{x}^{3}\\,dx\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(1-z)[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-z}}2x\\,dx]dz+{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1-z}}-2{x}^{3}\\,dx]dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(1-z)[{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{1-z}}dz+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{1-z}}dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(1-z)^{2}\\,dz-\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(1-z)^{2}\\,dz \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(1-z)^{2}\\,dz \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{[-(1-z)^{3}]}_{z=0}^{z=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527957 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133923 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4693bb81-f299-50fa-9cbd-3a5bb1c90da9" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Over a Type III Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10b3f812-017d-59eb-99e5-5a00f74bf7d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527344} {:answer/id #uuid "35e1c9bf-ea2b-560e-8f70-12de88c73f78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527418} {:answer/id #uuid "49e17673-b9ad-517c-bb9b-8d3f2668d8ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527452} {:answer/id #uuid "78e4424f-a2d2-5162-a013-91916d289fbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527534} {:answer/id #uuid "e438768b-4435-5fed-b94f-351a63a4645d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527756}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78e4424f-a2d2-5162-a013-91916d289fbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527534} :answer-field/id #uuid "3888cc3d-bb90-568c-bfd5-048cece1217d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527826}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7a83145c-370c-5913-b3c6-439072b6c354" :question/math-academy-id "q-161772" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}xyz\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the type III region given by \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le z\\le 2,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{4-2z},\\,0\\le y\\le x\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}xyz\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-2x}}{\\int }_{0}^{x}xyz\\,dy\\,dx\\,dz.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-2x}}{\\int }_{0}^{x}xyz\\,dy\\,dx\\,dz & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-2x}}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}xyz\\,dy]dx\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-2x}}xz{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}dx\\,dz \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-2x}}xz(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})\\,dx\\,dz \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-2x}}{x}^{3}z\\,dx\\,dz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x$, treating $z$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-2x}}{x}^{3}z\\,dx\\,dz & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}z[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-2z}}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}z \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}z{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{4-2z}}\\text{d}z \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{4}(4-2z)^{2}z\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}4z-4{z}^{2}+{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}4z-4{z}^{2}+{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\frac{1}{2}{[2{z}^{2}-\\frac{4}{3}{z}^{3}+\\frac{1}{4}{z}^{4}]}_{z=0}^{z=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(8-\\frac{32}{3}+4)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281358 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133925 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1889f67-327c-5e6e-b646-5bd58a244778" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing and Evaluating Triple Integrals Over Type III Regions From Diagrams"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d48cc3d-ead9-593f-915c-d3aaa480ed03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278715} {:answer/id #uuid "3e139408-c514-52b7-89df-e2b959afe3df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279139} {:answer/id #uuid "5e531d96-5cc8-51fb-a104-07e94c5bec18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279456} {:answer/id #uuid "c6bcddbb-ebc8-5c7b-ad03-f16d13624465" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280333} {:answer/id #uuid "cc2fc060-126f-54c6-ba8f-9f107326389f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280384}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d48cc3d-ead9-593f-915c-d3aaa480ed03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278715} :answer-field/id #uuid "544d160b-e29b-59aa-9938-64c90c8cfe69" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280972}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2dd43989-4160-5cb0-b938-4fe05b8b6278" :question/math-academy-id "q-161853" :question/problem "![](images/a1/a1e4a1e39c85a037f3f4f49910b651300363ef34bee969464f5e711aa00986e3.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}4{x}^{2}z\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the right one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](images/91/9165163be9ce95e7165f04d26e6ce8080699ab4d477eba3f804c849fdf1fb679.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type III region\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 4-z\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/ca/ca74bf149c1371fe9f1622586d9eb92fe180a9c9bb6a0c53d16f538b3c55f4a4.png)\n\nHence, the type III representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 4-z\\}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}4{x}^{2}z\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4-z}4{x}^{2}z\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4-z}4{x}^{2}z\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{4-z}4{x}^{2}z\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}4{x}^{2}z[y]_{y=0}^{y=4-z}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}4{x}^{2}z(4-z)\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(16{x}^{2}z-4{x}^{2}{z}^{2})\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(16{x}^{2}z-4{x}^{2}{z}^{2})\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}(16{x}^{2}z-4{x}^{2}{z}^{2})\\,dz]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[8{x}^{2}{z}^{2}-\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{2}{z}^{3}]_{z=0}^{z=3}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}36{x}^{2}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}36{x}^{2}\\,dx & ={[12{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(12-0) \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527935 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133925 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1889f67-327c-5e6e-b646-5bd58a244778" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing and Evaluating Triple Integrals Over Type III Regions From Diagrams"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b6f618c-bcbb-5ea7-9f0c-1e592526ff75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527425} {:answer/id #uuid "70deb780-c887-5dc9-85bd-f3b01ab2a24b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{128}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527519} {:answer/id #uuid "c0d3ac95-6cd9-512a-9fab-45c1bf14a2cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527697} {:answer/id #uuid "c4cd7a9d-8989-5c58-b2bd-dbc2dff6d515" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527700} {:answer/id #uuid "cd88dea5-2a41-5c70-9ba3-d70de53ad32d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527724}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70deb780-c887-5dc9-85bd-f3b01ab2a24b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{128}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527519} :answer-field/id #uuid "35cfb42e-572e-5b24-aa8c-8d68254f52ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527822}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "43d7c496-4713-50a7-87bb-4a90921bae35" :question/math-academy-id "q-161891" :question/problem "![](images/3c/3cba44923f4f583cf6e01ac87cdd6e5ca73a75993eef8322cd01bf44416f84f4.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}4x\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the right one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](images/f1/f112dd83a8cbb7563979dc170db23db7e178ba1762aca23fd4073c50e1c7a343.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type III region\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 5-x-z\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/71/71974fddc8e0e0b6a12fc6a248c15eea08c9f6b8a0823d50aede8aadc31a41fa.png)\n\nHence, the type III representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 5-x-z\\}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}4x\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{5-x-z}4x\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{5-x-z}4x\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{5-x-z}4x\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}4x[y]_{y=0}^{y=5-x-z}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}4x(5-x-z)\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(20x-4{x}^{2}-4xz)\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(20x-4{x}^{2}-4xz)\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}(20x-4{x}^{2}-4xz)\\,dz]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[20xz-4{x}^{2}z-2x{z}^{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(32x-8{x}^{2})\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(32x-8{x}^{2})\\,dx & ={[16{x}^{2}-\\frac{8{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(64-\\frac{64}{3})-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{128}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527916 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133925 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1889f67-327c-5e6e-b646-5bd58a244778" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing and Evaluating Triple Integrals Over Type III Regions From Diagrams"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d8a1e4b-eb13-5f55-ba55-4b5dc6ff93cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527405} {:answer/id #uuid "89ab1fef-8fcd-5fa1-bf90-fadaaa814b18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527578} {:answer/id #uuid "af68ffb6-0b68-527c-9426-425189a60c7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527666} {:answer/id #uuid "b4001b41-6468-5fa7-9631-47ce66435f95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527674} {:answer/id #uuid "d304075d-a560-5677-ac5a-03672fe435b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527732}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d8a1e4b-eb13-5f55-ba55-4b5dc6ff93cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527405} :answer-field/id #uuid "36d55e5e-4911-5da7-af48-d3ee67db6281" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527823}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0d6e2493-0d92-5bdf-8874-580184f51513" :question/math-academy-id "q-161932" :question/problem "![](images/6f/6f4bf1fe2f1a49f84b56702c4a83272c2f927ea4774eb677f43e525bf6cfb1f7.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}8x\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the right one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](images/71/71f3fd0cbbde8adeca71688d6b53e2cd4cdf72076be3efa770cfebb8c10ffb76.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type III region\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3-\\frac{3x}{4}-\\frac{z}{2}\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/cd/cd84968e9e5300a18d087ba566202aba2b7166818a590cca03eac90d4f3f7a89.png)\n\nHence, the type III representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3-\\frac{3x}{4}-\\frac{z}{2}\\}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}8x\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3-3x/4-z/2}8x\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3-3x/4-z/2}8x\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{3-3x/4-z/2}8x\\,dy]dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}8x[y]_{y=0}^{y=3-3x/4-z/2}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}8x(3-\\frac{3x}{4}-\\frac{z}{2})\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(24x-6{x}^{2}-4xz)\\,dz\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(24x-6{x}^{2}-4xz)\\,dz\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}(24x-6{x}^{2}-4xz)\\,dz]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[24xz-6{x}^{2}z-2x{z}^{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=3}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(72x-18{x}^{2}-18x)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(54x-18{x}^{2})\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(54x-18{x}^{2})\\,dx & ={[27{x}^{2}-6{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(27-6)-0 \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527974 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133925 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1889f67-327c-5e6e-b646-5bd58a244778" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing and Evaluating Triple Integrals Over Type III Regions From Diagrams"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "115cd6e6-10bc-511d-a50c-dda4391d3fbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3}2xz\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527345} {:answer/id #uuid "22edfedb-abf4-5e13-a50c-a2d93085d7f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}2xz\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527386} {:answer/id #uuid "3ae67555-8807-5b1f-a6b0-f964a1dc4b0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}x{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527424} {:answer/id #uuid "80a27c48-5897-5356-94fa-417faa7570de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527557} {:answer/id #uuid "f8bb3c60-8c7f-5dc8-99aa-dec23229dd1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2xz\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527790}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22edfedb-abf4-5e13-a50c-a2d93085d7f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}2xz\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527386} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbe73ac4-9782-563c-b73e-8c4d198957b7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527886}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9c0ba772-2d81-508b-bca4-4e2298a7113a" :question/math-academy-id "q-163509" :question/problem "![](images/33/335bf5e4e2a4ee9d0286eadb968e0e82c6afb18d47cd5258d6d1b6cee3d5c5a6.png)\n\nGiven that $R$ is the type III region shown above, \n${∭}_{R}xz\\,\\text{d}V=$" :question/worked-solution "For a type III region $R$ with projection $D$ onto the $xz$-plane, the triple integral of a continuous function $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,z)}^{{u}_{2}(x,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe consider the region $R$ as a type III region enclosed between the back surface $y={u}_{1}(x,z)=1$ and the front surface $y={u}_{2}(x,z)=3.$\n\n![](images/b1/b176bcf502a0801eae2bf470dfe4bf92852a34b06675fd74be78b30ccb4f6469.png)\n\nSo, the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,1\\le y\\le 3\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ as a type I *plane* region in the $xz$-plane with the upper curve\n\n$$\nz=1-{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\n![](images/eb/eb054b5f1567aa2c56842d79133fbbefc41a8b40730c688381d88e3ef06ccab7.png)\n\nHence, $D=\\{(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le 1-{x}^{2}\\}.$\n\nTherefore, we write the triple integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}xz\\,\\text{d}V & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{1}^{3}xz\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}[{\\int }_{1}^{3}xz\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}xz[y]_{y=1}^{y=3}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{x}^{2}}2xz\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527928 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133925 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1889f67-327c-5e6e-b646-5bd58a244778" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing and Evaluating Triple Integrals Over Type III Regions From Diagrams"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1777f129-2300-50d6-8d27-23f4df21de70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{z}^{2}}^{1}3\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527354} {:answer/id #uuid "44e017a0-acd0-5090-9f6b-fbd6846fc15e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}3\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527439} {:answer/id #uuid "9544c54c-0125-5d55-81cd-f694dc48efb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527604} {:answer/id #uuid "9efbc1c3-6631-5be2-8f9f-5c89d7338265" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{z}^{2}}^{1}2x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527634} {:answer/id #uuid "cadf3a5a-c92a-51ff-a1de-b3f65f160f80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{z}^{2}}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1777f129-2300-50d6-8d27-23f4df21de70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{z}^{2}}^{1}3\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527354} :answer-field/id #uuid "47db12a1-3244-5a01-bb35-553d717703fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527832}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3242c4d8-39d7-5463-b665-91b0cfa5917f" :question/math-academy-id "q-163715" :question/problem "![](images/5b/5b7552bbde56a68bfca44adb0501a4a4a8ae0a1105d3dc9039d05bfb6fd405c9.png)\n\nGiven that $R$ is the type III region shown above, \n${∭}_{R}2y\\,\\text{d}V=$" :question/worked-solution "For a type III region $R$ with projection $D$ onto the $xz$-plane, the triple integral of a continuous function $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,z)}^{{u}_{2}(x,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe consider the region $R$ as a type III region enclosed between the back surface $y={u}_{1}(x,z)=1$ and the front surface $y={u}_{2}(x,z)=2.$\n\n![](images/2f/2f1112a1fa4e540ce8ef2d1337383a2adcb378ba519cfb9c49a4521e5bc1b02f.png)\n\nSo, the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,1\\le y\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ as a type II *plane* region in the $xz$-plane with the left curve\n\n$$\nx={z}^{2}.\n$$\n\n![](images/2d/2dcbae12ed3351892c63117f86bab7ffe6e1818b7a16666b42c2efdcc6bd787f.png)\n\nHence, $D=\\{(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,{z}^{2}\\le x\\le 1\\}.$\n\nTherefore, we write the triple integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}2y\\,\\text{d}V & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}2y\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{z}^{2}}^{1}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}2y\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{z}^{2}}^{1}[{y}^{2}]_{y=1}^{y=2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{z}^{2}}^{1}3\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134287 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133916 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "40486856-137f-55c4-8464-f99e7e1c659f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Mixed Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26371e7c-d4aa-5cd0-a363-95439d905659" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324279} {:answer/id #uuid "4d153674-baf0-565f-a0eb-dec9cc52f8a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324608} {:answer/id #uuid "9a3d06d0-0635-568c-b9ca-dac6fef15963" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325283} {:answer/id #uuid "9b0a8c83-7180-5d2f-946a-f9b34a2d351d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325291} {:answer/id #uuid "d4882293-69d6-5858-b2d4-78dc60ebf4d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325820}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a3d06d0-0635-568c-b9ca-dac6fef15963" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325283} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6c48fd4-9172-51c8-a0ec-c24aea7453e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326519}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e6d26c08-ceec-5b48-a4a3-f3df87eec565" :question/math-academy-id "q-40403" :question/problem "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}2xyz\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\ngiven that the region $D$ in the $xz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{4-2z},\\,0\\le z\\le 2\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}2xyz\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}xz[{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{3}z\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type II region in the $xz$-plane.\nTherefore, to evaluate our double integral as a repeated integral over this region, we integrate with respect to $x$ and then with respect to $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{x}^{3}z\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-2z}}{x}^{3}z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}z[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-2z}}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}z{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{4-2z}}\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{4}(4-2z)^{2}z\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}4z-4{z}^{2}+{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={[2{z}^{2}-\\frac{4}{3}{z}^{3}+\\frac{1}{4}{z}^{4}]}_{z=0}^{z=2} \\\\  & =(8-\\frac{32}{3}+4)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134293 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133917 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf29db1b-f47b-53de-b31d-e4da1d0a9e5f" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Triple Integral as a Mixed or Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e2c97d4-b434-5053-9663-fa52d98d5684" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324100} {:answer/id #uuid "4b299549-5cb0-56d7-9c33-9a26cc8d61bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324580} {:answer/id #uuid "95a97664-7cb4-546a-9467-1efee24db627" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325246} {:answer/id #uuid "9ecaa195-92d6-5644-a84f-02c83f6bf09c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325317} {:answer/id #uuid "b67b4bdb-21a2-5cc7-a126-ffb05118dd40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b67b4bdb-21a2-5cc7-a126-ffb05118dd40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325537} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d2a35f2-61ae-55fb-8f9b-a4bff3e74ef2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326502}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f9f2f2a5-47b5-5a66-9153-5085ab9c95cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-40503" :question/problem "$$\n{∭}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx\n$$\n\nThe triple integral above is defined over the type III region given by\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le z\\le 2x+1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1+x+z\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "A type III region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(x,z)\\le y\\le {u}_{2}(x,z)\\}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type III region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/06/0603bed12c6af74e46544d8bebc52362aed95a9a5ad7418ea4faaf228f3b5241.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type III region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,z)}^{{u}_{2}(x,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(x,z)=0,\\,{u}_{2}(x,z)=1+x+z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{1+x+z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le z\\le 2x+1\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by expressing the double integral over $D$ as a repeated integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{1+x+z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2x+1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1+x+z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dz\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{2x+1}{\\int }_{0}^{1+x+z}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=(-1)+(2x+1)=2x.\n$$"}]}
